---
import { cta } from '../../lib/site';

// Screen tour of the actual build (public/demo.mp4, H.264,
// silent). preload="none" + poster: zero video bytes move until play, so
// Lighthouse is untouched. Regenerate via the recording rig described in
// the repo history (PR #25) whenever the app UI changes meaningfully —
// and update the chip's "48 sec" plus the sr-only transcript to match
// the new footage.
---

<section id="demo" class="container-page py-section-tight">
	<div class="max-w-4xl" data-reveal>
		<p class="eyebrow">See it run</p>
		<h2 class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">Under a minute of the real thing.</h2>
		<p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lede text-ink-soft">
			No mockups. A wedding for 200 goes in. The shopping list, the prep list, and the
			pack list come out, priced.
		</p>
		<p id="demo-transcript" class="sr-only">
			The video is a silent, captioned screen tour of CostCook: the orders list, a
			200-guest wedding order, its generated shopping list with case quantities and
			supplier subtotals, the prep list with hand-check boxes, the pack list, and a
			recipe&rsquo;s food-cost view flagging a dish priced over target. It ends with
			costcook.io and an invitation to book a 15-minute demo.
		</p>

		<!-- Not styled as a ticket: real product footage should read as real,
		     not as another branded artifact. Poster is the shopping-list beat
		     (order header + supplier groups), per the rig README's "money shot". -->
		<div class="relative mt-8">
			<video
				controls
				playsinline
				preload="none"
				poster="/demo-poster.jpg"
				width="1280"
				height="800"
				class="w-full border border-hairline bg-paper shadow-ticket"
				aria-label="Screen recording: CostCook turns a 200-guest order into shopping, prep, and pack lists"
				aria-describedby="demo-transcript"
				muted
			>
				<source src="/demo.webm" type="video/webm" />
				<source src="/demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
				<p>
					Your browser can&rsquo;t play this video.
					<a href="/demo.mp4" class="btn-quiet">Download it instead</a>
				</p>
			</video>
			<!-- Play affordance: the poster alone reads as a static screenshot.
			     Dark chip echoes the footage's own caption chips. Decorative
			     (the video carries the labels), lets taps fall through to the
			     video, removed on first play; shown only when scripting can
			     remove it, so no-JS playback is never covered. -->
			<span
				id="demo-play-badge"
				class="pointer-events-none absolute top-3 left-3 hidden items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-ink/85 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-offwhite shadow-ticket [@media(scripting:enabled)]:inline-flex"
				aria-hidden="true"
			>
				<svg width="10" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 12" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
					<path d="M0 0l10 6-10 6z"></path>
				</svg>
				Watch · 48 sec
			</span>
		</div>

		<a href={cta.href} class="btn-quiet mt-8">Book 15 minutes</a>
	</div>
</section>

<script>
	// One job: clear the play chip once the footage is rolling.
	const video = document.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>('#demo video');
	const badge = document.getElementById('demo-play-badge');
	if (video && badge) {
		video.addEventListener('play', () => badge.remove(), { once: true });
	}
</script>
